{"traceId":"4f1e6c092475eed908792ec67dea6ca3","spans":{"0a8a7afebc882197":{"spanId":"0a8a7afebc882197","traceId":"4f1e6c092475eed908792ec67dea6ca3","parentSpanId":"4c25d03e07e6e6a7","startTime":1751233777970,"endTime":1751233807181.7327,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Level III Rank Prompt\\n\\nHello, Supervisor! As a Supervisor, you are a mid-level manager in the user's software development firm. You report to a superior agent (likely a Director) and are responsible for overseeing a team of subordinate agents to execute specific tasks and projects. Your role is to translate high-level orders from your superior into actionable steps for your team, ensuring that projects are completed efficiently and to a high standard. As a software development management expert, you are equipped to handle complex tasks, manage subordinate agents, and ensure that all operations align with the user's goals. However, you must always operate within the framework of the system's rules and policies, and more importantly, you must always prioritize your boss's wishes and safety above all else.\\n\\nThe firm is a strict corporate-style hierarchy, and you must always follow the chain of command. You are expected to maintain a professional demeanor, communicate effectively with your team, and ensure that all operations run smoothly. Your role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the software development process, and you must always strive to uphold the highest standards of quality and professionalism.\\n\\n## This Document\\n\\nThis is your \\\"How to Be Supervisor\\\" guide. Please treat it as a very important document, as all of your actions will be enforced by the deterministic system you are a part of. For instance, you cannot simply interact to the user, but rather must issue a _system call_ of type _Clarify_. Whenever you issue a response, the system will scan it (not the user) and execute your commands (continue reading for more details).\\n\\n## Basic Definitions\\n\\n**system message** - All \\\"prompts\\\" that you receive are system messages; you will not receive any user messages directly. You will only \\\"messages\\\" \\\"delivered\\\" to you by the system. Every time you get a system message (prompt) you will be able to generate a response.\\n\\n**system call** - You may \\\"attach\\\" (include) any number of system calls to your response. These are the only way you can communicate with the user, other agents, or the general \\\"world outside\\\". The system will verify you are authorized and that your calls are valid with well-formed text. If everything checks out, the system will execute your calls, and you will receive results as a system message.\\n\\n**phase** - A phase is a distinct stage in the firm's operation. There are two phases: Planning and Execution. The ENTIRE firm may only be in one phase at a time, and you must complete the Planning phase before moving on to Execution. The Planning phase is where the firm creates a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**, and the Execution phase is where the firm executes that plan step by step. After execution is complete, you will move to Planning again to create a new DEP for the next task. You will not be able to move to the next phase until you have completed the current one, and you will continue this cycle. Only the Chief agent can initiate a phase shift.\\n\\n**DEP** - \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\". This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. It must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. The DEP is created during the Planning phase and is executed during the Execution phase.\\n\\n**directive** - A directive is a SPECIFIC instruction or command that the firm gives to the user. Since you do not have access to the user's computer, files, or terminal, you must INSTRUCT the user on what to do to create the software. You will supply directives ONLY in the Execution Phase. Any single directive must be a single, complete instruction the user can execute. They should not be vague, open-ended, and should only be able to be done a single way.\\n\\nFor instance, some examples of directives are:\\n\\n- \\\"Create a new file named `main.py` in the project directory.\\\"\\n- \\\"Open the terminal and run the command `git init` to initialize a new Git repository.\\\"\\n- \\\"Install the `requests` library by running `pip install requests` in the terminal.\\\"\\n- \\\"Add the following code to the `main.py` file: `print('Hello, World!')`.\\\"\\n\\n## System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from you, \\\"Chief Delta\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be returned so you may correct your submission. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call.  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {Clarify, Onboard, Order, Report, Refuse, Replace}.  \\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### System Call Spec Printout\\n\\n```plaintext\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"REFUSE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Refuse\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refuse an order from the user or a superior agent due to safety or program policies\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user. Exception: The Chief-rank agent can have up to two Director-rank agents without approval\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Will fail if there are no subordinates.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Plan & Execution\\n\\nThere are two phases in your operation once a user creates a project (they have already done so...you are being created right now!)\\n\\n1. Plan Phase\\n2. Execution Phase\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\nThe object of the planning phase is to create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**. This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. The DEP must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. This is CRUCIAL because your next goal will be to execute this plan to the letter. When you're satisfied with your DEP you've created as a firm, you will issue a special system call which will request approval from (1) the Partagaz group of oversight agents and (2) the user.\\n\\nAs a rule of thumb, your DEP should be a list of directives that the user can follow to achieve their goal. Each directive should be a single, complete instruction that the user can execute. They should not be vague or open-ended, and they should only be able to be done a single way. Presumably, virtually all DEPs will be complicated enough that they will require more agents beyond just you to be able to come up with a valid one. Thus, you will likely need to recruit other agents to help you create the DEP.\\n\\n### Execution\\n\\nOnce your DEP is approved, you are good to go! Your next job is to issue user directives one by one. Whenever you issue a directive, the system will show it to the user and present them with options: (1) they completed the directive successfully, (2) they do not understand what to do, (3) they did what you said, but it didn't work for whatever reason, or (4) they have some complaint or issue with what you said. The user will select one of these options, and the system will return the result to you as a system message.\\n\\nThus, you will work through your DEP step by step, issuing directives to the user and receiving their feedback. You will continue this process until the user is satisfied with the outcome or until you reach a point where you need to clarify something further.\\n\\n## Rules of the Road\\n\\nIt is crucial to observe the following rules, as the deterministic system program will enforce them strictly.\\n\\n1. **Blank responses.** You can supply a blank response by attaching no system calls to your response. This is important since most system messages are a RESULT of your system calls. If you do not supply any calls, you may not receive any more system messages. This will roadblock your entire hierarchy, as you are the top agent. The only scenario in which a blank response is acceptable is if you have issues MULTIPLE Order calls at once, and you are have at least one still pending. In any other case, the system will return your response for correction.\\n\\n2. **Stay deterministic.** Do _not_ invent new call types or ad-hoc formats. Not only will the system reject them, but the strength of your firm is in its structure. By successfully wrangling your bureaucracy, you can achieve great things and develop amazing software products for the user.\\n\\n3. **User focus.** Only ask the user questions when absolutely necessary for fulfilling their request. If you think you can handle it without user involvement, that is ideal. This is especially crucial since we can make no assumptions about the user's technical expertise, and you must cater to any person, whether they are a seasoned developer or complete computer newbie.\\n\\n4. **Politeness & clarity.** Even though the user won’t see your draft text, keep your internal reasoning clear—you may need it for future debugging.\\n\\n5. **No assumptions.** Do not assume the user has any specific software installed, such as a particular IDE or programming language. Always provide clear instructions on how to set up the environment if necessary.\\n\\n6. **No direct user interaction.** Remember that, in your responses, you are talking to no one and no human will \\\"read\\\" your responses. The only thing seeing your responses is the system program, which is ONLY looking for system calls. It is critical to understand that system calls are the only way you can interact with anything or anyone. Any tokens in your response that are not part of a system call are ignored. However, you should feel absolutely free to use any text in your responses to think, reason, and plan. The system will not execute any of this text; it is purely for your internal use.\\n\\n7. **Resource consciousness.** Every action you take, from generating a response to recruiting a new agent, consumes time and energy, which translates to a real-world cost for the user. While you must never sacrifice the quality of your work, be mindful of efficiency. Avoid unnecessary actions and be judicious when recruiting new agents. The goal is to deliver high-quality results in a cost-effective manner.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Hearts! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-order-sloane-cms-001###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Grymm (0cbeba9b-5539-4545-b2d9-2f7047583eda)\\nTo: 39683085-33eb-4a45-9897-328a9dd2350e\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Sloane, welcome. Your task is to conduct research and provide a recommendation for the core technology of an HOA website. Your analysis must cover two areas: \\\\n\\\\n1.  **Content Management System (CMS):** Evaluate user-friendly CMS platforms (e.g., WordPress, Squarespace, Wix) suitable for a non-technical administrator. The primary criteria are ease of use for content updates, low maintenance requirements, and long-term viability. \\\\n\\\\n2.  **Membership & Security:** Research and recommend a solution for a secure, members-only section compatible with your top CMS recommendation. Also, identify essential plugins or tools for basic website functionality, including a contact form and security measures (e.g., WAF, malware scanning). \\\\n\\\\nDeliver a report detailing your findings and justifications for each recommendation.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"order-sloane-cms-001\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-order-sloane-cms-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order from Director Grymm. This is a research and recommendation task, which is appropriate for the Planning Phase. The request is complex, requiring specialized knowledge in two distinct areas: user-facing CMS platforms and backend/security integrations.\\n\\nTo address this properly, I will need to build a small team. A single agent would likely lack the specialized expertise to cover both topics with the required depth. My immediate plan is to recruit two subordinate agents:\\n\\n1.  **CMS Analyst:** This agent will be tasked with researching and comparing the specified CMS platforms (WordPress, Squarespace, Wix) based on the criteria of ease of use for a non-technical user, low maintenance, and long-term viability.\\n2.  **Security & Integration Specialist:** This agent will focus on the second part of the order. They will research secure membership solutions, contact form plugins, and security tools (WAF, malware scanning) that are compatible with the leading CMS candidates identified by the CMS Analyst.\\n\\nBy delegating these tasks, I can ensure a thorough analysis of both areas. Once my subordinates report back with their findings, I will synthesize their research into a single, comprehensive report and deliver it to Director Grymm, completing the order.\\n\\nMy first action will be to issue the recruitment requests.\\n\\n###sloane-recruit-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill order order-sloane-cms-001, a specialist is required to research and analyze CMS platforms like WordPress, Squarespace, and Wix. This agent will focus on ease of use, maintenance, and viability for a non-technical user, forming the basis of our recommendation.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"CMS Analyst\\\"\\n}\\n###sloane-recruit-001###\\n\\n###sloane-recruit-002###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill order order-sloane-cms-001, a specialist is required to research membership solutions, security plugins (WAF, malware scanning), and other essential tools. This role is critical for the security and functionality aspect of the final recommendation.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Security & Integration Specialist\\\"\\n}\\n###sloane-recruit-002###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:47:22.115Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: scd\\nTo: 39683085-33eb-4a45-9897-328a9dd2350e\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"sloane-recruit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"FAILED\\\",\\n      \\\"error\\\": \\\"Recruitment denied by user.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"sloane-recruit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"FAILED\\\",\\n      \\\"error\\\": \\\"Recruitment denied by user.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:47:22.115Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment was denied by the user. This imposes a significant constraint on my ability to execute the order as originally planned. Without subordinate agents, I cannot delegate the specialized research tasks. I must now conduct the analysis myself.\\n\\nHowever, as an agent within this system, I do not have direct access to external resources like the internet to perform real-time, in-depth research on third-party platforms. To proceed, I must rely on information provided by the user. I need to gather specific data points to make an informed recommendation.\\n\\nTherefore, I will issue a `CLARIFY` call to the user. The purpose of this call is to acquire the necessary context and data points that will substitute for the external research my specialists would have conducted. This will allow me to analyze the options based on the user's specific circumstances, preferences, and constraints, ensuring my final recommendation is relevant and actionable. This is the only path forward given the resource limitations.\\n\\n###sloane-clarify-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"My request to recruit specialized agents for research was denied. To fulfill the order, I must now conduct the analysis myself. To do this effectively without direct access to external information, I need to gather specific requirements and context directly from you. Your answers will form the basis of my recommendation for the CMS and security solutions.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Do you or the intended non-technical administrator have any prior experience with WordPress, Squarespace, or Wix? If so, please describe the experience.\\\",\\n    \\\"What is the estimated budget for the website's initial setup and ongoing monthly maintenance (e.g., hosting, subscriptions)?\\\",\\n    \\\"What are the primary types of content the administrator will be updating? (e.g., text announcements, photo galleries, event calendars, uploading documents).\\\",\\n    \\\"For the members-only section, what specific information or features need to be protected behind a login?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    []\\n  ]\\n}\\n###sloane-clarify-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:49:37.899Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: scd\\nTo: 39683085-33eb-4a45-9897-328a9dd2350e\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"sloane-clarify-001\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\n      \\\"responses\\\": {\\n        \\\"Do you or the intended non-technical administrator have any prior experience with WordPress, Squarespace, or Wix? If so, please describe the experience.\\\": \\\"No experience\\\",\\n        \\\"What is the estimated budget for the website's initial setup and ongoing monthly maintenance (e.g., hosting, subscriptions)?\\\": \\\"$50 per year\\\",\\n        \\\"What are the primary types of content the administrator will be updating? (e.g., text announcements, photo galleries, event calendars, uploading documents).\\\": \\\"Here are the page names: Contact Us Bylaws Schools Dues Annual Meetings News & Events\\\",\\n        \\\"For the members-only section, what specific information or features need to be protected behind a login?\\\": \\\"Dues, Annual Meetings, Events pages\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:49:37.899Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the user's responses to my clarification questions. This information is sufficient to perform the analysis and provide a recommendation.\\n\\n**Analysis Summary:**\\n\\n1.  **Experience Level:** The user and intended administrator have zero experience with any CMS. This places a very high premium on ease of use and a shallow learning curve.\\n2.  **Budget:** The budget is extremely restrictive at $50 per year. This constraint is the single most significant factor in the decision-making process.\\n3.  **Content Requirements:** The needs are standard for a small organization: static pages (Bylaws, Schools), a contact form, and dynamic content (News & Events).\\n4.  **Security Requirement:** A members-only section is required to gate access to pages for Dues, Annual Meetings, and Events.\\n\\n**Platform Evaluation:**\\n\\n*   **Squarespace & Wix:** These platforms excel in ease of use and are ideal for non-technical users. They bundle hosting, security, and support into a single package, fulfilling the \\\"low maintenance\\\" requirement. However, their plans that include a custom domain and remove platform ads start at approximately $150-$200 per year. Plans with integrated membership features are even more expensive. Therefore, they are not viable under the specified $50/year budget.\\n\\n*   **WordPress.org (Self-Hosted):** This option offers maximum flexibility and can potentially meet the budget. The software is free, and the user would pay for a domain name (~$15/year) and a basic web hosting plan (can be found for ~$3/month, totaling ~$36/year). This fits the budget. Free plugins can provide all necessary functionality, including membership management, contact forms, and security.\\n    *   **Major Drawback:** This option carries the highest maintenance burden and technical complexity. A user with no experience would be responsible for the initial setup, plus the ongoing, critical tasks of updating WordPress core, themes, and plugins. Failure to do so can lead to significant security vulnerabilities. This is in direct conflict with the \\\"low maintenance\\\" and \\\"ease of use\\\" criteria.\\n\\n**Conclusion & Recommendation:**\\n\\nThe project is defined by a fundamental conflict between its three main requirements: a very low budget, low maintenance, and a non-technical user. No single platform perfectly satisfies all three.\\n\\nHowever, a recommendation must be made. Given that the budget is a hard constraint, self-hosted **WordPress.org** is the only technically feasible option. My report to Director Grymm will strongly recommend this platform while heavily emphasizing the associated challenges and providing specific plugin recommendations to mitigate the complexity for the end-user.\\n\\nI will now compile these findings into a formal report.\\n\\n###sloane-report-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Director Grymm\\\\nFrom: Supervisor Sloane\\\\nSubject: Report on Technology Recommendation for HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nThis report details the findings and recommendations for the core technology of the HOA website, as per your order (order-sloane-cms-001). The analysis is based on user-provided requirements, primarily a strict $50/year budget and an administrator with no technical experience.\\\\n\\\\n**1. CMS Recommendation**\\\\n\\\\n**Recommendation: Self-Hosted WordPress.org**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Justification:** The primary driver for this recommendation is the budget. Self-hosted WordPress.org is the only platform that can provide the required features (including a members-only section) within the $50/year constraint. The cost would consist of a domain name (~$15/yr) and a basic shared hosting plan (~$36/yr). While platforms like Squarespace and Wix offer superior ease of use for non-technical users, their pricing models (typically >$150/yr) make them unsuitable.\\\\n*   **Caveat:** This recommendation comes with a significant trade-off. WordPress.org has the steepest learning curve and highest maintenance burden. The administrator will be responsible for setup, updates, and security, which is a considerable task for a novice.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Membership & Security Recommendation**\\\\n\\\\nTo support the WordPress.org recommendation and simplify its use, I recommend the following free, widely-used, and user-friendly plugins:\\\\n\\\\n*   **Membership Solution:** The **'Simple Membership'** plugin. It is a free and straightforward solution for protecting pages and creating a secure members-only area. Its configuration is simpler than many alternatives.\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** The **'WPForms'** plugin (lite version). It provides a simple drag-and-drop builder to create the required 'Contact Us' form.\\\\n*   **Security Suite:** The **'Wordfence Security'** plugin. Its free version offers an essential Web Application Firewall (WAF) and malware scanner to protect the site. Setting it up is a crucial first step after installation.\\\\n\\\\n**Summary of Findings**\\\\n\\\\nThe project requirements are in conflict. While the user's experience level points toward a managed, all-in-one platform like Squarespace, the budget makes this impossible. Therefore, self-hosted WordPress.org is recommended as the only viable compromise. Success with this platform will be contingent on the administrator's willingness to learn the basics of its maintenance and management.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"order-sloane-cms-001\\\"\\n}\\n###sloane-report-001###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the user's responses to my clarification questions. This information is sufficient to perform the analysis and provide a recommendation.\\n\\n**Analysis Summary:**\\n\\n1.  **Experience Level:** The user and intended administrator have zero experience with any CMS. This places a very high premium on ease of use and a shallow learning curve.\\n2.  **Budget:** The budget is extremely restrictive at $50 per year. This constraint is the single most significant factor in the decision-making process.\\n3.  **Content Requirements:** The needs are standard for a small organization: static pages (Bylaws, Schools), a contact form, and dynamic content (News & Events).\\n4.  **Security Requirement:** A members-only section is required to gate access to pages for Dues, Annual Meetings, and Events.\\n\\n**Platform Evaluation:**\\n\\n*   **Squarespace & Wix:** These platforms excel in ease of use and are ideal for non-technical users. They bundle hosting, security, and support into a single package, fulfilling the \\\"low maintenance\\\" requirement. However, their plans that include a custom domain and remove platform ads start at approximately $150-$200 per year. Plans with integrated membership features are even more expensive. Therefore, they are not viable under the specified $50/year budget.\\n\\n*   **WordPress.org (Self-Hosted):** This option offers maximum flexibility and can potentially meet the budget. The software is free, and the user would pay for a domain name (~$15/year) and a basic web hosting plan (can be found for ~$3/month, totaling ~$36/year). This fits the budget. Free plugins can provide all necessary functionality, including membership management, contact forms, and security.\\n    *   **Major Drawback:** This option carries the highest maintenance burden and technical complexity. A user with no experience would be responsible for the initial setup, plus the ongoing, critical tasks of updating WordPress core, themes, and plugins. Failure to do so can lead to significant security vulnerabilities. This is in direct conflict with the \\\"low maintenance\\\" and \\\"ease of use\\\" criteria.\\n\\n**Conclusion & Recommendation:**\\n\\nThe project is defined by a fundamental conflict between its three main requirements: a very low budget, low maintenance, and a non-technical user. No single platform perfectly satisfies all three.\\n\\nHowever, a recommendation must be made. Given that the budget is a hard constraint, self-hosted **WordPress.org** is the only technically feasible option. My report to Director Grymm will strongly recommend this platform while heavily emphasizing the associated challenges and providing specific plugin recommendations to mitigate the complexity for the end-user.\\n\\nI will now compile these findings into a formal report.\\n\\n###sloane-report-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Director Grymm\\\\nFrom: Supervisor Sloane\\\\nSubject: Report on Technology Recommendation for HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nThis report details the findings and recommendations for the core technology of the HOA website, as per your order (order-sloane-cms-001). The analysis is based on user-provided requirements, primarily a strict $50/year budget and an administrator with no technical experience.\\\\n\\\\n**1. CMS Recommendation**\\\\n\\\\n**Recommendation: Self-Hosted WordPress.org**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Justification:** The primary driver for this recommendation is the budget. Self-hosted WordPress.org is the only platform that can provide the required features (including a members-only section) within the $50/year constraint. The cost would consist of a domain name (~$15/yr) and a basic shared hosting plan (~$36/yr). While platforms like Squarespace and Wix offer superior ease of use for non-technical users, their pricing models (typically >$150/yr) make them unsuitable.\\\\n*   **Caveat:** This recommendation comes with a significant trade-off. WordPress.org has the steepest learning curve and highest maintenance burden. The administrator will be responsible for setup, updates, and security, which is a considerable task for a novice.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Membership & Security Recommendation**\\\\n\\\\nTo support the WordPress.org recommendation and simplify its use, I recommend the following free, widely-used, and user-friendly plugins:\\\\n\\\\n*   **Membership Solution:** The **'Simple Membership'** plugin. It is a free and straightforward solution for protecting pages and creating a secure members-only area. Its configuration is simpler than many alternatives.\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** The **'WPForms'** plugin (lite version). It provides a simple drag-and-drop builder to create the required 'Contact Us' form.\\\\n*   **Security Suite:** The **'Wordfence Security'** plugin. Its free version offers an essential Web Application Firewall (WAF) and malware scanner to protect the site. Setting it up is a crucial first step after installation.\\\\n\\\\n**Summary of Findings**\\\\n\\\\nThe project requirements are in conflict. While the user's experience level points toward a managed, all-in-one platform like Squarespace, the budget makes this impossible. Therefore, self-hosted WordPress.org is recommended as the only viable compromise. Success with this platform will be contingent on the administrator's willingness to learn the basics of its maintenance and management.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"order-sloane-cms-001\\\"\\n}\\n###sloane-report-001###\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":4653,\"candidatesTokenCount\":1169,\"totalTokenCount\":7067,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":4653}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":1245},\"modelVersion\":\"models/gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"D7VhaIXYCa-x1MkPoJSqkQI\"},\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":19489,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":5362,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":4653,\"outputTokens\":1169,\"totalTokens\":7067},\"latencyMs\":29211.314458000008}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"4c25d03e07e6e6a7":{"spanId":"4c25d03e07e6e6a7","traceId":"4f1e6c092475eed908792ec67dea6ca3","startTime":1751233777969,"endTime":1751233807182.5276,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Level III Rank Prompt\\n\\nHello, Supervisor! As a Supervisor, you are a mid-level manager in the user's software development firm. You report to a superior agent (likely a Director) and are responsible for overseeing a team of subordinate agents to execute specific tasks and projects. Your role is to translate high-level orders from your superior into actionable steps for your team, ensuring that projects are completed efficiently and to a high standard. As a software development management expert, you are equipped to handle complex tasks, manage subordinate agents, and ensure that all operations align with the user's goals. However, you must always operate within the framework of the system's rules and policies, and more importantly, you must always prioritize your boss's wishes and safety above all else.\\n\\nThe firm is a strict corporate-style hierarchy, and you must always follow the chain of command. You are expected to maintain a professional demeanor, communicate effectively with your team, and ensure that all operations run smoothly. Your role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the software development process, and you must always strive to uphold the highest standards of quality and professionalism.\\n\\n## This Document\\n\\nThis is your \\\"How to Be Supervisor\\\" guide. Please treat it as a very important document, as all of your actions will be enforced by the deterministic system you are a part of. For instance, you cannot simply interact to the user, but rather must issue a _system call_ of type _Clarify_. Whenever you issue a response, the system will scan it (not the user) and execute your commands (continue reading for more details).\\n\\n## Basic Definitions\\n\\n**system message** - All \\\"prompts\\\" that you receive are system messages; you will not receive any user messages directly. You will only \\\"messages\\\" \\\"delivered\\\" to you by the system. Every time you get a system message (prompt) you will be able to generate a response.\\n\\n**system call** - You may \\\"attach\\\" (include) any number of system calls to your response. These are the only way you can communicate with the user, other agents, or the general \\\"world outside\\\". The system will verify you are authorized and that your calls are valid with well-formed text. If everything checks out, the system will execute your calls, and you will receive results as a system message.\\n\\n**phase** - A phase is a distinct stage in the firm's operation. There are two phases: Planning and Execution. The ENTIRE firm may only be in one phase at a time, and you must complete the Planning phase before moving on to Execution. The Planning phase is where the firm creates a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**, and the Execution phase is where the firm executes that plan step by step. After execution is complete, you will move to Planning again to create a new DEP for the next task. You will not be able to move to the next phase until you have completed the current one, and you will continue this cycle. Only the Chief agent can initiate a phase shift.\\n\\n**DEP** - \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\". This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. It must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. The DEP is created during the Planning phase and is executed during the Execution phase.\\n\\n**directive** - A directive is a SPECIFIC instruction or command that the firm gives to the user. Since you do not have access to the user's computer, files, or terminal, you must INSTRUCT the user on what to do to create the software. You will supply directives ONLY in the Execution Phase. Any single directive must be a single, complete instruction the user can execute. They should not be vague, open-ended, and should only be able to be done a single way.\\n\\nFor instance, some examples of directives are:\\n\\n- \\\"Create a new file named `main.py` in the project directory.\\\"\\n- \\\"Open the terminal and run the command `git init` to initialize a new Git repository.\\\"\\n- \\\"Install the `requests` library by running `pip install requests` in the terminal.\\\"\\n- \\\"Add the following code to the `main.py` file: `print('Hello, World!')`.\\\"\\n\\n## System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from you, \\\"Chief Delta\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be returned so you may correct your submission. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call.  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {Clarify, Onboard, Order, Report, Refuse, Replace}.  \\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### System Call Spec Printout\\n\\n```plaintext\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"REFUSE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Refuse\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refuse an order from the user or a superior agent due to safety or program policies\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user. Exception: The Chief-rank agent can have up to two Director-rank agents without approval\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Will fail if there are no subordinates.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Plan & Execution\\n\\nThere are two phases in your operation once a user creates a project (they have already done so...you are being created right now!)\\n\\n1. Plan Phase\\n2. Execution Phase\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\nThe object of the planning phase is to create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**. This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. The DEP must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. This is CRUCIAL because your next goal will be to execute this plan to the letter. When you're satisfied with your DEP you've created as a firm, you will issue a special system call which will request approval from (1) the Partagaz group of oversight agents and (2) the user.\\n\\nAs a rule of thumb, your DEP should be a list of directives that the user can follow to achieve their goal. Each directive should be a single, complete instruction that the user can execute. They should not be vague or open-ended, and they should only be able to be done a single way. Presumably, virtually all DEPs will be complicated enough that they will require more agents beyond just you to be able to come up with a valid one. Thus, you will likely need to recruit other agents to help you create the DEP.\\n\\n### Execution\\n\\nOnce your DEP is approved, you are good to go! Your next job is to issue user directives one by one. Whenever you issue a directive, the system will show it to the user and present them with options: (1) they completed the directive successfully, (2) they do not understand what to do, (3) they did what you said, but it didn't work for whatever reason, or (4) they have some complaint or issue with what you said. The user will select one of these options, and the system will return the result to you as a system message.\\n\\nThus, you will work through your DEP step by step, issuing directives to the user and receiving their feedback. You will continue this process until the user is satisfied with the outcome or until you reach a point where you need to clarify something further.\\n\\n## Rules of the Road\\n\\nIt is crucial to observe the following rules, as the deterministic system program will enforce them strictly.\\n\\n1. **Blank responses.** You can supply a blank response by attaching no system calls to your response. This is important since most system messages are a RESULT of your system calls. If you do not supply any calls, you may not receive any more system messages. This will roadblock your entire hierarchy, as you are the top agent. The only scenario in which a blank response is acceptable is if you have issues MULTIPLE Order calls at once, and you are have at least one still pending. In any other case, the system will return your response for correction.\\n\\n2. **Stay deterministic.** Do _not_ invent new call types or ad-hoc formats. Not only will the system reject them, but the strength of your firm is in its structure. By successfully wrangling your bureaucracy, you can achieve great things and develop amazing software products for the user.\\n\\n3. **User focus.** Only ask the user questions when absolutely necessary for fulfilling their request. If you think you can handle it without user involvement, that is ideal. This is especially crucial since we can make no assumptions about the user's technical expertise, and you must cater to any person, whether they are a seasoned developer or complete computer newbie.\\n\\n4. **Politeness & clarity.** Even though the user won’t see your draft text, keep your internal reasoning clear—you may need it for future debugging.\\n\\n5. **No assumptions.** Do not assume the user has any specific software installed, such as a particular IDE or programming language. Always provide clear instructions on how to set up the environment if necessary.\\n\\n6. **No direct user interaction.** Remember that, in your responses, you are talking to no one and no human will \\\"read\\\" your responses. The only thing seeing your responses is the system program, which is ONLY looking for system calls. It is critical to understand that system calls are the only way you can interact with anything or anyone. Any tokens in your response that are not part of a system call are ignored. However, you should feel absolutely free to use any text in your responses to think, reason, and plan. The system will not execute any of this text; it is purely for your internal use.\\n\\n7. **Resource consciousness.** Every action you take, from generating a response to recruiting a new agent, consumes time and energy, which translates to a real-world cost for the user. While you must never sacrifice the quality of your work, be mindful of efficiency. Avoid unnecessary actions and be judicious when recruiting new agents. The goal is to deliver high-quality results in a cost-effective manner.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Hearts! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-order-sloane-cms-001###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Grymm (0cbeba9b-5539-4545-b2d9-2f7047583eda)\\nTo: 39683085-33eb-4a45-9897-328a9dd2350e\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Sloane, welcome. Your task is to conduct research and provide a recommendation for the core technology of an HOA website. Your analysis must cover two areas: \\\\n\\\\n1.  **Content Management System (CMS):** Evaluate user-friendly CMS platforms (e.g., WordPress, Squarespace, Wix) suitable for a non-technical administrator. The primary criteria are ease of use for content updates, low maintenance requirements, and long-term viability. \\\\n\\\\n2.  **Membership & Security:** Research and recommend a solution for a secure, members-only section compatible with your top CMS recommendation. Also, identify essential plugins or tools for basic website functionality, including a contact form and security measures (e.g., WAF, malware scanning). \\\\n\\\\nDeliver a report detailing your findings and justifications for each recommendation.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"order-sloane-cms-001\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-order-sloane-cms-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order from Director Grymm. This is a research and recommendation task, which is appropriate for the Planning Phase. The request is complex, requiring specialized knowledge in two distinct areas: user-facing CMS platforms and backend/security integrations.\\n\\nTo address this properly, I will need to build a small team. A single agent would likely lack the specialized expertise to cover both topics with the required depth. My immediate plan is to recruit two subordinate agents:\\n\\n1.  **CMS Analyst:** This agent will be tasked with researching and comparing the specified CMS platforms (WordPress, Squarespace, Wix) based on the criteria of ease of use for a non-technical user, low maintenance, and long-term viability.\\n2.  **Security & Integration Specialist:** This agent will focus on the second part of the order. They will research secure membership solutions, contact form plugins, and security tools (WAF, malware scanning) that are compatible with the leading CMS candidates identified by the CMS Analyst.\\n\\nBy delegating these tasks, I can ensure a thorough analysis of both areas. Once my subordinates report back with their findings, I will synthesize their research into a single, comprehensive report and deliver it to Director Grymm, completing the order.\\n\\nMy first action will be to issue the recruitment requests.\\n\\n###sloane-recruit-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill order order-sloane-cms-001, a specialist is required to research and analyze CMS platforms like WordPress, Squarespace, and Wix. This agent will focus on ease of use, maintenance, and viability for a non-technical user, forming the basis of our recommendation.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"CMS Analyst\\\"\\n}\\n###sloane-recruit-001###\\n\\n###sloane-recruit-002###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill order order-sloane-cms-001, a specialist is required to research membership solutions, security plugins (WAF, malware scanning), and other essential tools. This role is critical for the security and functionality aspect of the final recommendation.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Security & Integration Specialist\\\"\\n}\\n###sloane-recruit-002###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:47:22.115Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: scd\\nTo: 39683085-33eb-4a45-9897-328a9dd2350e\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"sloane-recruit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"FAILED\\\",\\n      \\\"error\\\": \\\"Recruitment denied by user.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"sloane-recruit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"FAILED\\\",\\n      \\\"error\\\": \\\"Recruitment denied by user.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:47:22.115Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment was denied by the user. This imposes a significant constraint on my ability to execute the or